-advice-for-job-seekers)\\n7. [6\\\\. Regional Spotlights](https://managementconsulted.com/consulting-industry-monthly-market-review-may-2025/#6-regional-spotlights)\\n8. [7\\\\. Future Outlook and Key Trends to Watch](https://managementconsulted.com/consulting-industry-monthly-market-review-may-2025/#7-future-outlook-and-key-trends-to-watch)\\n9. [Next Steps](https://managementconsulted.com/consulting-industry-monthly-market-review-may-2025/#next-steps)\\n\\nFurther Reading\\n\\n- [2025 Top Consulting Firms](https://managementconsulted.com/top-consulting-firms/)\\n- [2025 Consulting Salaries](https://managementconsulted.com/consultant-salary/)\\n- [2025 Application Deadlines](https://managementconsulted.com/consulting-application-deadlines/)\\n- [2025 Case Interview Guide](https://managementconsulted.com/case-interview/)\\n- [2025 Case Frameworks Guide](https://managementconsulted.com/case-interview-frameworks/)\\n- [2025 Consulting Resume Guide](https://managementconsulted.com/consulting-resume/)\\n- [2025 Storytelling Guide](https://managementconsulted.com/pyramid-principle/)\\n- [Consulting Firm Directory](https://managementconsulted.com/consulting-firm-directory/)\\n\\n## **Executive Summary**\\n\\nThe management consulting industry in May 2025 continues to show **steady resilience** despite broader economic uncertainty. While overall corporate spending remains strong in key sectors like technology, and healthcare, firms are **prioritizing specialist hires** over generalist expansion. Digital transformation, supply chain resilience, cost optimization, and AI strategy remain high-demand areas.\\n\\n![PwC updated logo](https://assets.managementconsulted.com/app/uploads/2025/05/30142511/pwc_20250430113802_original_image_19.webp)The "new" PwC logo - what do you think?\\n\\nThe upcoming entry-level recruiting season is on pace to exceed last year\\\'s, while lateral hiring for niche expertise is heating up.\\n\\n**Key Changes from April:**\\n\\n- The number of job openings in management consulting and corporate strategy on our [Job Board](http://jobs.managementconsulted.com/) increased by over 10%.\\n- [PwC rebrands](https://www.marketingweek.com/pwc-rebrand-brand-platform/) (kinda).\\n- M&A activity picks up. [Infosys will acquire Houston-based energy consultancy MRE Consulting](https://www.consulting.us/news/11727/infosys-to-acquire-houston-based-mre-consulting); [IBM buys AI and data consultancy Hakkoda](https://www.consulting.us/news/11673/ibm-buys-data-and-ai-consultancy-hakkoda).\\n\\nGet this month\\\'s consulting industry insights\\n\\nWhat\\\'s happening in the industry today? What is signal and what is noise? How - if at all - should you respond? Get your report today.\\n\\nEmail\\n\\nYes, Send My Free Report!\\n\\n## **1\\\\. Industry Pulse: Economic and Market Drivers**\\n\\n**Macroeconomic Conditions:**\\n\\n- **U.S. GDP shrunk at an annualized rate of 0.3% in Q1**, although final sales to private domestic purchasers, which tracks demand from businesses and consumers, rose at a 3% rate (up from 2.9% in Q4 2024).\\n- **The March 2025 headline U.S. inflation rate** (the latest figure available as of print time) eased to 2.4%, compared to 2.8% in February 2025. The core inflation rate, which excludes volatile food and energy prices, was 2.8%, the lowest in 4 years.\\n- According to [The Guardian](https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/apr/28/trump-tariffs-shipments-us-ports), **U.S. freight volumes are plummeting** \\\\- "figures show the number of vessels scheduled to arrive at the Port of Los Angeles next week is [down by almost a third](https://volumes.portoptimizer.com/) compared to the same period last year." Separately, data provider Financial Times from Vizion reports that container bookings from China to the U.S. fell 45% by mid-April compared with 2024.\\n\\n**Private Equity Activity:**\\n\\n- **The hoped for rebound in deal volume hasn\\\'t materialized yet in 2025**. According to [Ropes & Gray](https://www.ropesgray.com/en/insights/alerts/2025/03/us-pe-market-recap), YTD dealmaking through the first two months of this year was lower than the same period in any of the last 5 years. This has major implications for firms who specialize in commercial due diligence and PE value creation projects.\\n\\n**Technology Adoption:**\\n\\n- AI-related initiatives (strategy, risk management, ethics) are fueling new consulting engagements.\\n\\n**Regulatory Environment:**\\n\\n- Shifting global trade policy is increasing **demand for geopolitical and trade consulting services**, as large manufacturers and distributors aim to shift supply chains, optimize inventory levels, and develop new pricing strategies. Our [Top 10 Trade Consulting Firms](https://managementconsulted.com/top-international-trade-consulting-firms-poised-to-benefit-from-a-trade-war/) are poised to benefit and firms (e.g., Kearney) are actively staffing up in these areas.\\n\\n## **2\\\\. Consulting Firm Activity Highlights**\\n\\n**Bain & Company** announced [its pledge](https://www.bain.com/about/media-center/press-releases/20252/bain--companys-social-impact-pledge-%242-billion-in-pro-bono-consulting-by-2035/) to provide over $2 billion in pro bono consulting services by 2035.\\n\\n**BCG** CEO Christoph Schweizer was re-elected to a 2nd, 4-year term.\\n\\n**Deloitte** will [move its North American headquarters](https://www.wsj.com/real-estate/commercial/deloitte-office-hudson-yards-manhattan-4a55d495) to Hudson Yards in Manhattan, occupying ~800,000 square feet of a new 1.1 million-square-foot tower. Amenities will include on-site event space, high-end restaurants, and "red eye rooms" to help employees getting off flights recover faster. This is exciting news for Deloitte employees who will be based in New York, as well as for the ultra high-end office market in the U.S. It\\\'s also another confirmation that many firms in the industry are re-emphasizing in-person office attendance.\\n\\n[**Unity Advisory**](https://unity-advisory.com/) launched operations - the new firm, helmed by former EY and PwC leaders, aims to compete against the Big Four in the UK and European markets initially. The firm will focus on serving upper middle-market businesses without the conflict of interest it says is inherent to the Big Four business model.\\n\\n**PwC rebranded** to [align its image](https://www.marketingweek.com/pwc-rebrand-brand-platform/) with an increased focus on AI and digital transformation, and it comes at a potentially good time, as the firm was recently fined by Chinese and UK regulatory authorities. The Saudi Public Investment Fund also [suspended its involvement with the firm](https://www.arabnews.com/node/2598766). Reaction to the rebrand has been [mixed](https://www.instagram.com/reel/DJE1whpO-45/?igsh=OXdvejh5OWx5N3Rs).\\n\\n**The Department of Government Efficiency** (DOGE) has affected up to $20B in consulting contracts. [Read our breakdown](https://managementconsulted.com/doge-and-u-s-government-cut-at-least-1-5b-in-consulting-spend/) of who is affected the most, or [listen to the podcast version](https://managementconsulted.com/podcast/doge-cuts-1-5b-consulting-spend/).\\n\\n**Firms including Alvarez & Marsal, BCG, L.E.K., McKinsey** and more are [hiring now](http://jobs.managementconsulted.com/) \\\\- especially in North America, and especially for specialist or senior roles. Many open roles are concentrated in the **Healthcare and Life Sciences** space, citing rising demand for healthcare operational excellence in the midst of disruption. If you\\\'re a job seeker, create a [free profile](https://jobs.managementconsulted.com/registration/job-seeker) on our job board today.\\n\\n**Huron Consulting** sources tell us that the firm continues to experience rapid growth, and is hiring across its [practice areas](https://www.huronconsultinggroup.com/company/careers) (healthcare, education, digital transformation)\\n\\n![Related\\\'s new Hudson Yards office tower](https://assets.managementconsulted.com/app/uploads/2025/04/30141343/im-70740995.avif)A rendering of Deloitte\\\'s swanky new digs. Photo: Related Companies\\n\\n## **3\\\\. Talent Market Update**\\n\\n**Hiring Trends:**\\n\\n- Lateral hiring strong for AI specialists, trade experts, education consultants, Oracle / Workday SMEs, and those with industrials / healthcare experience.\\n- Campus recruiting will begin earlier; [MBB application deadlines are already published](https://managementconsulted.com/consulting-application-deadlines/), and we expect interviews to begin in mid to late July.\\n\\n**In-Demand Skillsets:**\\n\\n- AI literacy and machine learning strategy\\n- Supply chain resilience\\n- Corporate restructuring and cost optimization\\n- Education policy\\n- Trade barrier / tariff proficiency\\n\\n**Salary Trends:**\\n\\n- Lateral candidates with AI or trade expertise can command a ~**10% salary premium**.\\n- Candidates recruiting through on-campus channels or those with non-premium experience have **no room to negotiate**.\\n\\n**Workplace Considerations:**\\n\\n- Bench time is decreasing in major public sector consulting practices, and in some cases, if consultants can\\\'t get staffed on new projects immediately, they are being laid off. MC COO Namaan Mian spoke to [HR Brew](https://www.hr-brew.com/stories/2025/04/11/what-layoffs-at-consultancies-like-deloitte-mean-for-recruiters) about this recently.\\n- In commercial practices, our sources indicate consultant utilization is increasing from 2024 levels. This could be a leading indicator of increased attrition as we head into H2 2025.\\n\\n## **4\\\\. Consulting Skills in Demand**\\n\\n**Technical:**\\n\\n- Generative AI consulting frameworks\\n- Advanced analytics and data storytelling\\n- Supply chain digitalization and optimization\\n\\n**Soft Skills:**\\n\\n- [Executive presence](https://managementconsulted.com/power-presentation/) in virtual and hybrid settings\\n- Hypothesis-driven problem-solving\\n- Client relationship management in uncertain markets\\n\\n## **5\\\\. Candidate Watch: Advice for Job Seekers**\\n\\n**Focus on specialization as a lateral hire:** Candidates who demonstrate expertise in AI, trade, or cost optimization have a stronger edge.\\n\\n**Prepare for hybrid interviews:** Many first-round interviews remain virtual, but superdays and final rounds are increasingly in-person. Virtual interviews require you to be [overly structured and overly communicative](https://managementconsulted.com/virtual-case-interview/).\\n\\n**Expect digital assessments:** Firms are increasingly asking candidates to solve [digital assessments](https://managementconsulted.com/mckinsey-digital-assessment/) in advance of first round interview invites.\\n\\n**Students - begin prep now:** Resume drops for undergraduate and specialty masters students targeting Summer 2026 start dates begin in early July. You should be [80% prepared for interviews](https://managementconsulted.com/black-belt/) by the time you apply.\\n\\n21\\n\\nDay\\n\\n21\\n\\nHr\\n\\n16\\n\\nMin\\n\\n05\\n\\nSec\\n\\nTime is running out for the June[Black Belt](https://managementconsulted.com/black-belt/ "")\\xa0cohort (limited seats are available).\\n\\nAdd To Cart\\n\\n## **6\\\\. Regional Spotlights**\\n\\n**North America:**\\n\\n- Chicago and Boston showing strong lateral hiring activity.\\n- DC hiring slowing as public sector practices see reduced demand.\\n\\n**Europe:**\\n\\n- London market continues to see growth; financial services consulting in demand.\\n- Paris emerging as digital transformation hub.\\n\\n**Middle East:**\\n\\n- Dubai, Doha, Abu Dhabi, and Riyadh offices continue to see strong demand for consulting services (although lower than peak demand earlier this decade). Much of this demand is concentrated in infrastructure, energy, and economic diversification work.\\n\\n**Asia-Pacific:**\\n\\n- Manufacturing consulting firms seeing uptick in demand in response to global trade environment.\\n- We expect to see some capital inflows into Australia\\\'s bond market as some capital exits the U.S.\\n\\n## **7\\\\. Future Outlook and Key Trends to Watch**\\n\\nContinued strength in **AI strategy**, **digital transformation**, and **cost optimization** projects.\\n\\n**Boutique consulting firms** continue to gain market share as clients seek nimble, specialist providers.\\n\\n**Hiring uptick** expected to persist through Q4 as economic uncertainty drives demand for consulting services.\\n\\n**Geopolitical risks** (e.g., China-U.S. tensions, global elections) are a net positive for the industry.\\n\\n## Next Steps\\n\\nDo you currently work at a consulting firm? We’re gathering insights from management consultants to understand current industry sentiment, emerging trends, and overall market outlook. Your responses are anonymous and will help create a more accurate picture of the state of the industry. [Take a short survey here](https://forms.gle/SG1wQPWkMVhd5te9A).\\n\\n[![Team-Training-1.jpg](https://c03d53.managementconsulted.com/users/92cd8de35b2a/images/fca57b4d609c1726002922-Team-Training-1.jpg?width=3360)](https://managementconsulted.com/team-training/)\\n\\n[Back to blogs](https://managementconsulted.com/articles/)\\n\\n### Save your cart?\\n\\nx\\n\\nNotifications\\n\\n[iframe](blob:https://managementconsulted.com/4bbc1ef0-2baf-4b32-b892-517828563a6a)\\n\\n[iframe](https://www.google.com/recaptcha/api2/anchor?ar=1&k=6LecaYUUAAAAAEWUhBcHa2DzRArs62Wi1e6259se&co=aHR0cHM6Ly9tYW5hZ2VtZW50Y29uc3VsdGVkLmNvbTo0NDM.&hl=en&v=X-oVtzDcTGjZVms4LEgykmCV&size=invisible&cb=cfr2t9z1ws49)\\n\\n## Contact us\\n\\nWe\\\'re not currently able to chat, but would love to connect!\\n\\n\\\\\\\\* indicates a required field\\n\\nName\\\\*Required Asterisksignifies that this field can not be left blank\\n\\nEmail\\\\*Required Asterisksignifies that this field can not be left blank\\n\\nWe\\\'re not around but we still want to hear from you! Leave us a note:\\\\*Required Asterisksignifies that this field can not be left blank\\n\\nSend\\n\\n[powered by Olark Logo](http://www.olark.com/live-chat-powered-by-olark)\\n\\nOlark launch button clip path\\n\\nContact us\\n\\n[iframe](https://www.google.com/recaptcha/api2/anchor?ar=1&k=6LecaYUUAAAAAEWUhBcHa2DzRArs62Wi1e6259se&co=aHR0cHM6Ly9tYW5hZ2VtZW50Y29uc3VsdGVkLmNvbTo0NDM.&hl=en&v=X-oVtzDcTGjZVms4LEgykmCV&size=invisible&cb=6xe75j28vm0q)\\n\\n[iframe](https://www.google.com/recaptcha/api2/bframe?hl=en&v=X-oVtzDcTGjZVms4LEgykmCV&k=6Lf7eJwUAAAAAGthwqDeh2T1gzO9vyNioHv7eJf0)\', \'metadata\': {\'ogTitle\': \'Consulting Market Overview - May 2025\', \'robots\': [\'noai, noimageai\', \'index, follow, max-image-preview:large, max-snippet:-1, max-video-preview:-1\'], \'article:modified_time\': \'2025-05-02T14:52:33+00:00\', \'og:image:type\': \'image/png\', \'et-api-origin\': \'https://managementconsulted.com\', \'og:type\': \'article\', \'language\': \'en-US\', \'viewport\': \'width=device-width\', \'og:image:width\': \'1792\', \'ogImage\': \'https://assets.managementconsulted.com/app/uploads/2025/05/01085616/Consulting-Market-Overview.png\', \'ogSiteName\': \'Management Consulted\', \'og:title\': \'Consulting Market Overview - May 2025\', \'modifiedTime\': \'2025-05-02T14:52:33+00:00\', \'og:image\': \'https://assets.managementconsulted.com/app/uploads/2025/05/01085616/Consulting-Market-Overview.png\', \'ogDescription\': \'Executive Summary The management consulting industry in May 2025 continues to show steady resilience despite broader economic uncertainty. While overall\', \'google-site-verification\': [\'LaS4XIO8eXYJ3yu7otLZt_jrb57Sn1P-DOxowXucJec\', \'w5gQQZ23Fv4xUR16Ymh27a2f0e3oMDsaoaYjY22DHw8\'], \'og:description\': \'Executive Summary The management consulting industry in May 2025 continues to show steady resilience despite broader economic uncertainty. While overall\', \'twitter:label2\': \'Est. reading time\', \'twitter:site\': \'@mconsulted\', \'twitter:data1\': \'Namaan Mian\', \'ogUrl\'